(1) Prevention of violence against women as referred to in Article 5 letter a shall be carried out in an integrated manner coordinated by the Regional Apparatus having the main duties and functions in the field of women's empowerment and child protection.
(2) Prevention as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be carried out by involving:
a. family;
b. community;
c. private sector;
d. community institutions;
e. social institutions; and
f. educational institutions.

Article 3
The protection of women and children victims of violence is implemented based on the principles of:
a. gender responsiveness;
b. non-discrimination;
c. equal and respectful relationships;
d. maintaining privacy and confidentiality;
e. providing a sense of safety and comfort;
f. respecting individual differences;
g. non-judgmental;
h. respecting the choices and decisions of victims;
i. sensitivity to the background and condition of victims;
j. use of language that is appropriate and understood by the victim;
k. fast and simple;
l. empathy; and
m. best interests of the victim.

Article 9
(1) Forms of protection services for women victims of violence include: a. legal aid services;
b. health services;
c. social rehabilitation services;
d. repatriation and social reintegration services;
e. complaint, consultation, and counseling services; and/or f. assistance services.
(2) Protection services for women as referred to in paragraph (1) include receiving and sending case referrals from or to other service units in a networked manner.
(3) Implementation of protection services for women as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be carried out by Regional Apparatus having main duties and functions in the field of women's empowerment.
(4) Further provisions regarding the forms and procedures for protection services for women victims of violence shall be regulated by a Regent Regulation.

Article 24
The duties and functions of FPKK as referred to in Article 23 paragraph (2) consist of:
a. coordinating and synchronizing prevention, services, and empowerment for women and children victims of violence;
b. maintaining and developing FPKK in the prevention, services, and empowerment of victims of violence through networking and a referral system;
c. conducting education on non-discrimination values towards women and children;
d. conducting socialization of laws and regulations related to the implementation of protection for women and children victims of violence;
e. collecting, compiling, and presenting reports of data on victims of violence; and
f. conducting monitoring and evaluation of the implementation of protection for women and children victims of violence.

REGENT OF SLEMAN,

Considering : a. that in order to restore the dignity and honor of women and children victims of violence and to restore their social function, it is necessary to undertake efforts for protection, empowerment of women, and rehabilitation of child victims of violence;
b. that based on Article 12 of Law 23 of 2014 concerning Regional Government, empowerment of women and protection of children constitute mandatory governmental affairs for regional governments;
c. that based on the considerations as referred to in letter a and letter b, it is necessary to establish a Regional Regulation concerning Protection of Women and Children Victims of Violence;

In View of : 1. Article 18 paragraph (6) of the 1945 Constitution of the Republic of Indonesia;
2. Law Number 15 of 1950 concerning the Establishment of Regency Regions within the Special Region of Yogyakarta (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 1950 Number 44);
3. Law Number 23 of 2002 concerning Child Protection (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2002 Number 109, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4235) as amended by Law Number 35 of 2014 concerning Amendment to Law Number 23 of 2002 concerning Child Protection (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 297, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5606) as amended by Government Regulation in Lieu of Law of the Republic of Indonesia Number 1 of 2016 concerning Second Amendment to Law Number 23 of 2002 concerning Child Protection (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2016 Number 99, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5882);
4. Law Number 23 of 2004 concerning the Elimination of Domestic Violence (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2004 Number 95, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 4419);
5. Law Number 23 of 2014 concerning Regional Government (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2014 Number 244, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5587) as last amended by Law Number 9 of 2015 concerning Second Amendment to Law Number 23 of 2014 concerning Regional Government (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2015 Number 58, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 5679);
6. Government Regulation Number 32 of 1950 concerning Stipulation of the Effective Date of Laws Number 12, 13, 14 and 15 concerning the Establishment of Regency Regions in East/Central/West Java and the Special Region of Yogyakarta (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 1950 Number 59);
7. Government Regulation Number 4 of 2006 concerning Implementation and Cooperation for Recovery of Victims of Domestic Violence (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Year 2006 Number 15, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 64);
8. Regional Regulation of the Special Region Province of Yogyakarta Number 3 of 2012 concerning Protection of Women and Children Victims of Violence (Regional Gazette of the Special Region Province of Yogyakarta Year 2012 Number 3, Supplement to the Regional Gazette of the Special Region Province of Yogyakarta Year 2012 Number 3);
9. Regional Regulation of Sleman Regency Number 18 of 2013 concerning Implementation of Child Protection (Regional Gazette of Sleman Regency Year 2013 Number 4 Series E, Supplement to the Regional Gazette of Sleman Regency Number 79);

With Mutual Approval

Article 8
(1) Protection services for women as referred to in Article 5 letter b are provided to women residents of the Region and/or women who experience violence where the incident occurred within the Region.
(2) The implementation of protection services for women is carried out with the principles of:
a. prompt;
b. safe;
c. empathy;
d. non-discrimination;
e. easily accessible; and
f. confidentiality is guaranteed.

CHAPTER VII
COMMUNITY PARTICIPATION
Article 25
(1) The community may participate in the protection of Victims.
(2) Community participation as referred to in paragraph (1) is carried out through:
a. provision of safe houses and/or shelters;
b. establishment and management of orphanages for children;
c. establishment of child rehabilitation centers;
d. active supervision of violence against women and children and reporting to the competent authorities;
e. providing first aid to victims;
f. reporting the occurrence of violence against women and children and providing protection;
g. forming family partners at the village level by the community; and
h. other forms of community participation related to the implementation of protection of women and protection of children.

